  "tour.advisor.title": "Solver advisor",
  "tour.advisor.p1": "On the Runs tab you can ask for advice before launching: an AI model reads the knowledge base and an anonymized description of your problem and suggests which solvers and parameters to use at each stage and what to watch. You can edit the parameters and apply them to the run — the launch is always confirmed by you.",
  "tour.advisor.p2": "Every dataset carries an attribute (the chip next to the advisor): 'local only' — the recommendation is produced by the local model and nothing leaves the machine (the default for uploads); 'any model' — a cloud model may also be used. Either way only anonymized aggregates are sent, never the data itself.",
  "tour.kb.title": "Solver-selection knowledge base",
  "tour.kb.p1": "The knowledge base is always a local document of recommendations: which solvers and approaches to use for pairing and rostering, how to split the work and which parameters to set. How it lives:",
  "tour.kb.i1": "It is built on the Test stand by a cloud AI model from public benchmarks (the external contour — open data only).",
  "tour.kb.i2": "On Stage and Prod the same local copy of the document is read by the local model — customer data never leaves the machine (the internal contour).",
  "tour.kb.i3": "For datasets marked 'any model' a cloud model may also read the base — it receives only the anonymized problem descriptor.",
  "tour.kb.p2": "Administrators get the Knowledge base tab: the document, its version and provenance, and a rebuild on Test. A visual contour diagram is in Demo 4.",
  "demo.launch4.title": "Demo 4 — knowledge base and AI contours",
  "demo.launch4.body": "How the solver-selection knowledge base is built and how the contours are separated: external AI models — only the Test stand and public data; inside — the local model. A diagram plus the path of a recommendation to human confirmation.",
  "da.intro": "The knowledge base is always a local document. The diagram shows where external and local AI models operate and why customer data never leaves the machine.",
  "da.s1.title": "Diagram: contour separation",
  "da.s1.body": "Left — the external contour (Test stand, open data only): a cloud model builds the knowledge base from public benchmarks. Right — the internal contour (Stage/Prod): the local model advises from the same local copy of the base.",
  "da.s1.note": "Only the knowledge-base file crosses the contour boundary (an ordinary code deploy) — and, for 'any model' datasets, the anonymized descriptor.",
  "da.s2.title": "Dataset attribute: L or C",
  "da.s2.body": "Every dataset carries an attribute that says which AI model may work with it.",
  "da.s2.l": "'Local only' (L) — customer data: the recommendation is produced by the local model only, nothing is sent out. The default for every upload.",
  "da.s2.c": "'Any model' (C) — openly published datasets (e.g. our benchmarks): a cloud model may be used, and even it receives only the anonymized descriptor.",
  "da.s2.desc": "The descriptor is aggregates only — no personal data:",
  "da.s3.title": "Recommendation and confirmation",
  "da.s3.body": "The model reads the knowledge base and the descriptor and suggests how to solve the problem: engines per stage, work split, parameters and warnings. A sample recommendation:",
  "da.s3.m.stage1": "column generation (GLOP + CP-SAT), duty pricer, gerad profile",
  "da.s3.m.stage2": "Timefold (Kotlin), late acceptance",
  "da.s3.m.warn": "check the stage-2 verdict after the run; the recommendation is valid for the current rule set",
  "da.s3.toast": "In the real UI the parameters would be filled into the launch form",
  "da.s3.note": "The recommendation is advisory: parameters can be edited and a human performs the launch. The live advisor is on the Runs tab.",
