  "tour.gdz.title": "Disruption: rapid roster repair",
  "tour.gdz.p1": "When something breaks after the solve — a sick pilot, a grounded aircraft — time works against you. The Board has a Disruption mode: mark the sick crew member and their days become hard unavailability for every check.",
  "tour.gdz.p2": "The Repair plan greedily covers the broken pairings with the minimum number of changes: free reserves first, then legal moves and swaps. Suboptimal — but done in seconds, legal, and reversible in one click.",
  "tour.gdz.p3": "Phase B is flight surgery: cancellations, aircraft pulls and delays dissolve the affected pairings. Rebuild creates a repair instance: column generation (CP-SAT) re-generates the neighbourhood, the untouched world is frozen by Timefold pins, the solver re-assigns the new pairings — and you get a before → after report. Phase C finishes off the uncoverable: adjacent pairings are unfrozen in rounds, and a no-progress round honestly rolls back.",
  "demo.launch9.title": "Disruption & rapid repair",
  "demo.launch9.body": "A sick call or last-minute re-crew: minimal changes in seconds.",
  "ddz.intro": "The schedule is computed and published — and then a pilot calls in sick or an aircraft is pulled from the line. How COSMOS repairs the roster in seconds to minutes while changing as little as possible.",
  "ddz.s1.title": "The disruption hits",
  "ddz.s1.body": "Last minute: a crew member is unavailable, flights at risk. We mark the sickness on the Board.",
  "ddz.s1.flow": "Solve published → Pilot sick → Days blocked → Pairings broken",
  "ddz.s1.e1": "EMP004 sick January 1–31",
  "ddz.s1.e2": "Sick days are hard unavailability for every check",
  "ddz.s1.e3": "Board: 13 pairings highlighted red",
  "ddz.s2.title": "Stability over optimality",
  "ddz.s2.body": "After a disruption what matters is not a perfect cost but minimal churn: crews hate reshuffles of a published roster.",
  "ddz.s2.e1": "The same legality rules as the board: aircraft type, base, rest, overlaps",
  "ddz.s2.e2": "Greedy repair: free reserves first, lowest credit first",
  "ddz.s2.e3": "No direct option? A swap: free a candidate with one legal move",
  "ddz.s2.note": "Classic crew recovery: Lettovský (2000), the Continental system (2003).",
  "ddz.s3.title": "The repair plan",
  "ddz.s3.body": "Seconds later — the plan: who covers whom, how, and how much changes.",
  "ddz.s3.flow": "Broken 13 → Changes 13 → Crew affected 6 → Violations 13 → 0",
  "ddz.s3.e1": "Every move is legal; every intermediate step too",
  "ddz.s3.e2": "The fewest people affected; healthy crews' pins are sacred",
  "ddz.s3.e3": "Anything uncovered is shown honestly in red — no silent holes",
  "ddz.s4.title": "Apply and move on",
  "ddz.s4.body": "The plan lands as reversible board edits: Reset edits restores everything.",
  "ddz.s4.e1": "Applied: 13 changes, 0 violations",
  "ddz.s4.e2": "Reversible: the moves show on the board, in the cabinet and in the pay card",
  "ddz.s4.e3": "Next — phase B: what if the flights themselves are cancelled?",
  "ddz.s4.note": "The hands-on lesson lives in Help → Training → Disruption: rapid repair.",
  "ddz.s5.title": "Phase B: the flights themselves are gone",
  "ddz.s5.body": "An aircraft is pulled — flights are cancelled or shifted. No re-assignment fixes that: the pairings themselves are dissolved. Surgery is needed.",
  "ddz.s5.flow": "Aircraft pulled → Flights cancelled → Pairings dissolved → Surviving legs pooled",
  "ddz.s5.e1": "Event: cancel LEG_29_1, LEG_01_6 (or a tail number + date window)",
  "ddz.s5.e2": "Affected pairings dissolved; their surviving legs go to the re-cover pool",
  "ddz.s5.e3": "Column generation (CP-SAT) rebuilds only the neighbourhood — in seconds",
  "ddz.s6.title": "Pins: the untouched world is frozen",
  "ddz.s6.body": "Merged catalog: untouched pairings ride through as-is, crew attached, under a Timefold pin. The solver assigns only the new ones.",
  "ddz.s6.e1": "199 of 201 pairings pinned with their crew — the solver cannot move them",
  "ddz.s6.e2": "Timefold assigned the 2 new pairings within a minute; greedy fallback if no solver",
  "ddz.s6.e3": "Before → after report: dissolved, new, uncovered — and a repair instance on the Board",
  "ddz.s6.note": "Numbers from a live run on GERAD benchmark #1: 201 pairings, 2 cancelled flights, ~70 seconds.",
  "ddz.s7.title": "Phase C: neighbourhood expansion",
  "ddz.s7.body": "The narrow neighbourhood may fail to cover every surviving leg. Then adjacent untouched pairings — same aircraft type, a stitch point nearby — are unfrozen and the columns are rebuilt.",
  "ddz.s7.flow": "Uncovered legs → Find stitch points → Unfreeze neighbours → New column round",
  "ddz.s7.e1": "Round 1: 4 legs proven uncoverable in the narrow pool",
  "ddz.s7.e2": "8 adjacent pairings unfrozen over 2 rounds; a no-progress round rolls back",
  "ddz.s7.e3": "Result: uncovered 4 → 2, survivors' pins 191/191, 22 new pairings crewed",
  "ddz.s7.note": "Live run on GERAD #1: 3 rounds, ~75 seconds end to end. The remaining 2 legs are uncoverable even in the expanded pool — the report says so honestly.",
  "learn.ch.c_dz.title": "Disruption: rapid repair",
  "learn.ch.c_dz.desc": "Sickness is repaired in place by the greedy plan; cancellations, aircraft pulls and delays — by a pinned neighbourhood rebuild in a repair instance.",
  "learn.c_dz.s1": "Disruptions are repaired on the Board. The lesson picks an instance with a ready roster itself — edits always sit on top of the engine solution and are reversible.",
  "learn.c_dz.s2": "The Disruption… button opens the rapid-repair panel. Open it — you get the sickness form, the active-events list and the plan buttons.",
  "learn.c_dz.s3": "The sickness form: employee, from–to dates, a note. After Mark sick their days become hard unavailability and the board highlights broken pairings in red. (The lesson does not mark anyone — this is live data.)",
  "learn.c_dz.s4": "Repair plan greedily covers the damage with the minimum of changes: free reserves → legal moves → swaps. The plan shows who covers whom, the stats and — honestly — anything uncovered.",
  "learn.c_dz.s5": "Apply plan lands the changes as reversible board edits. Reset edits returns the roster to the engine solution at any moment.",
  "learn.c_dz.s6": "Below are the flight-level events (phase B): Cancelled flights, Aircraft out of service (tail number + date window) and Flight delay. Such events dissolve every pairing touching those flights — the summary shows up in the Flight surgery line.",
  "learn.c_dz.s7": "Rebuild (plan B) creates a repair instance: the neighbourhood is re-generated by column generation (CP-SAT), untouched pairings are frozen with their crew (Timefold pins), and the solver re-assigns only the new ones. What the narrow pool cannot cover is treated by expansion (phase C): adjacent untouched pairings are unfrozen in rounds, and a no-progress round rolls back. You get a before → after report with the expansion line and a button opening the repair instance. (Not started in the lesson — the job runs 1–3 minutes.)",
  "learn.c_dz.s8": "Summary: sickness is repaired in place by the greedy plan (reversibly), while cancellations/aircraft/delays are repaired by a rebuild in a repair instance: minimal churn, pins hold the untouched world, anything uncovered is honestly listed. Two tools for two scales of disruption.",
  "ui.how": "How this screen works",
  "html.dz.toggle": "Disruption…",
  "html.dz.h": "Disruption: sickness / urgent re-crew",
  "html.dz.p": "Mark a sick crew member — their days become hard unavailability for the board and every check. \"Repair plan\" greedily covers the broken pairings with the minimum number of changes: free reserves first, then legal moves and swaps. The plan is applied as reversible board edits; anything uncovered is shown honestly in red.",
