  "cruns.help.p": "A run is the record of a computation over a task package from CDPM: the current run receives the package (via the channel or an upload), keeps every pairing and rostering attempt with its VMP and IDAK checks, and a passport — what it was computed with and on. A new package in the current run does not erase the previous one: it stays in the run's history together with its attempts. Any finished attempt can be replayed from the journal (byte for byte) or afresh.",
